Subject: [PATCH 0004/0012] present decoded frames through a Wayland surface

The frame producer exports the decoder's DMA-BUF (plane offsets, strides and
the duplicated handle) through the FFI, and the interface owns a Wayland
surface of its own that turns each export into a `wl_buffer` with
`zwp_linux_dmabuf_v1` and commits it. Nothing is converted on the GPU: the
compositor samples the decoder's NV12 planes directly.

The surface is created on the GUI thread with the connection quiet and posts
frames from the render thread. The buffer is described at its visible height
even when the decoder pads the picture, and the development capture hook
(interface screenshot, first frame) stays available behind its environment
variables.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [STM32MP25 performance work]

